::SECTION_63_TELEMETRY_LOG_ROTATION_AND_JSONL::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-LOG-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "High-Volume JSONL Telemetry Append & Size-Bounded Log Rotation (e:\\dl)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Disk exhaustion from runaway telemetry logs, torn half-written JSON lines on crash, or file-lock collisions during rotation"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Appending unbuffered lines without checking file size thresholds, or renaming an active log handle still open in another process."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Write complete newline-terminated JSON records in single atomic `WriteFile` calls with `FILE_APPEND_DATA`, rotate logs before exceeding `MAX_LOG_BYTES` (e.g., 16MB), and prune oldest archives beyond `MAX_LOG_GENERATIONS`."
}

::SECTION_64_MULTI_MONITOR_AND_OFFSCREEN_BOUNDS::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-MON-002] {
    DOMAIN          : "Multi-Monitor Workspace Coordinates & Off-Screen Window Restoration (MonitorFromRect / GetMonitorInfoW)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Saved holographic or console windows spawning completely off-screen after disconnecting a secondary monitor or changing resolution"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Restoring persisted `(X, Y)` window coordinates directly via `SetWindowPos` without validating intersection against active `MONITORINFO.rcWork` bounds."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Validate restored window rects with `MonitorFromRect(&rc, MONITOR_DEFAULTTONULL)`; if null or clipped outside `rcWork`, clamp coordinates inside the primary monitor's work area."
}

::SECTION_65_LOCAL_LLM_KV_CACHE_AND_CONTEXT_PRUNING::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-KV-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Local LLM Context Window Saturation & KV-Cache Sliding/Pruning (FireGem / Qwen GGUF Runtimes)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Sudden inference halt (`n_past >= n_ctx`), severe token-per-second degradation, or silent truncation of system instructions"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Appending conversation turns indefinitely into the KV cache without tracking `n_past` capacity or pinning the initial system prompt tokens."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Track active KV token count before `llama_decode()`, pin tokens `[0 .. n_keep)` for system/AVIS rules, and shift/evict older conversational KV blocks via `llama_kv_cache_seq_rm` + `seq_add` before hitting `n_ctx`."
}

::MASTER_VERIFICATION_GATE::
@GATE_CHECK_V29 {
    65. JSONL_ATOMIC_ROTATE : Enforce single-call `FILE_APPEND_DATA` writes and size-capped log rotation inside `e:\\dl`.
    66. WORKAREA_CLAMP      : Verify restored window coordinates intersect a live monitor `rcWork` via `MonitorFromRect`.
    67. KV_CACHE_PINNING    : Pin `[0 .. n_keep)` system prompt tokens and evict stale KV ranges before `n_past` reaches `n_ctx`.
}
